      'Do not discharge the child from care pending this examination when AHT is suspected — coordinate directly and immediately with the child\'s pediatrician, the emergency department, or the hospital-based child protection team rather than deferring the eye exam to a later, separate visit',
      'Understand and act on the fact that mandatory reporting to child protective services is a legal obligation that attaches once reasonable suspicion of abuse exists — it is not contingent on certainty, on completing every element of the workup, or on the examiner personally concluding that abuse occurred',
