      'Multilayered retinal hemorrhages extending from the posterior pole to the periphery, and traumatic retinoschisis, are the two findings most specific for AHT among the range of pediatric causes of retinal hemorrhage — but specificity is not the same as exclusivity, and the finding must be interpreted alongside the rest of the clinical picture, not in isolation.',
      'Birth-related retinal hemorrhage is common after vaginal delivery but resolves quickly — the large majority clear within about two to four weeks, with most gone within the first one to two weeks — so a comparable hemorrhage pattern persisting well beyond the neonatal period, or newly appearing in an infant past that window, should not be attributed to birth without a clear timeline supporting it.',
